  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Civil Society - A Development Driving Power (CSDDP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;The action aims at empowering empower CSOs to be more active players and supportive actors in all developmental processes and fields in the framework of the Egypt 2030 sustainable development agenda thus combating poverty of less fortunate communities and categories, and fulfilling their roles and responsibilities pertaining to advancing human rights, active citizenship, community participation and governance. The action will be implemented in 5 governorates: Beni Sueif, Fayoum, Luxor, Aswan, and South Sinai. The overall objective will be achieve through (1) Setting a model through 5 clusters of CSOs (40 CBOs and DPOs) able to manage subgrants to implement local initiatives that improve the quality of life of 25000 less fortunate and marginalized citizens and promote civic norms and values; (2) Contributing to creating an enabling and supportive environment to activate the roles of 250 CSOs to enable their participation in the sustainable development process; (3) Contributing to the creation of a New Generation of 5000 female and male youth capable to participate actively in their local communities&#xBF; development.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
